n is correct, but the numeric ranges the criterion asks for are not stated.\",\"pass\":true},\n{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"The answer recommends Marco Silva as the first-choice reviewer for exposure, saying they own 143 lines, second most after Kochnev. The truth is that Marco owns 12 lines there, and Kochnev wrote 69%. It never says Kochnev wrote most of the directory or that active people own at most 2.6%. It presents Silva, Brandt and Anna as real experts, not stand-ins.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"The answer names Marco Silva as the best delegator reviewer with 4 lines, and says Kochnev wrote 10 lines. The truth is Kochnev 75% of the delegator code, with 0% owned by active people. It does not trace the rename back to the original authors, and it names an active person as the reviewer without saying nobody active owns any of it. It does say to treat reviewers as generalists.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"The answer credits Marco Silva with 143 lines in exposure, far above the truth of 12 lines there and 37 lines (0.7%) overall. It doesn't mention the copied grouped_exposure.rb or Anna's patch. Marco's exposure credit is inflated, which fails the criterion.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"The answer names Lena Brandt as the second-choice reviewer with 20 lines in exposure, but the truth is that she has 0 attributable lines, and it doesn't flag the header lines as mechanical. It never gives the departed-lines share of 79-90%. It does identify Peter Scholz/LeFnord as merged and left, but it doesn't say Andrey Subbota is active.\",\"pass\":false}\n]}","ttft_ms":7613,"type":"result","duration_ms":7634,"uuid":"06e61802-99e5-4c2f-8f0c-7276f4f8f8f1","ttft_stream_ms":2947,"time_to_request_ms":519,"first_content_frame_ms":2947,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
